# 9. Above ₹3K

Our original user instruction says:

> "Anything above ₹3K, ask me."

So:

```text
Mandate:
automatic threshold = ₹3K
```

If the agent encounters:

```text
₹4,500
```

it should **not call `POST /payments` and hope it gets rejected**.

Instead:

```text
LLM
 ↓
₹4,500 > automatic threshold
 ↓
Ask user
```

If the user approves, we need a separate **one-off authorization mechanism**.

That's the next API design we need to settle, because I don't want to accidentally make the original reusable mandate silently expandable.

